  "caveats": [
    "Completion span for overlap includes independent CPU work before collecting GPU completion.",
    "Cycles measure calling-thread execution cost, not CPU percentage, power or driver threads.",
    "Explicit query counts exclude internal wait probes. A wait invocation does not prove an OS sleep.",
    "Tail waits are appropriate only when no intermediate CPU result is needed.",
    "Batch collection releases the completed prefix and waits for the first pending sequence without waiting to fill a batch.",
    "A same-queue ordering benchmark does not show concurrent kernels or compatible-GEMM merging.",
    "No fixed GPU clock; retain adjacent polling controls and apply a 3% drift limit.",
    "The full Strata native adapter and Linux GPU validation remain unfinished.",
    "Serial mode has no stable pair in the final run; its apparent slowdown has no stable percentage estimate.",
    "Prefix collection reports completed work; frozen-list/allocation lifetime and the whole-queue CPU-access restriction remain unchanged.",
    "Mode order is fixed and GPU clocks are not locked. Adjacent controls constrain drift but do not remove all mode-dependent clock/wakeup effects.",
    "The earlier short v1 run is retained as exploratory evidence and is not pooled with the final run."
  ],
